{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00969",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 2.05,
      "end_seconds": 19.98,
      "duration_seconds": 17.93,
      "text": "Quick one, doctor, I've another appointment at the optician. It's my hearing aids. I can't hear the television, even with them in, and my wife says I've got it up so loud the neighbours complain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.11,
      "end_seconds": 29.59,
      "duration_seconds": 6.48,
      "text": "I'll be quick, but let's get this right. Which ear is worse?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.05,
      "end_seconds": 40.21,
      "duration_seconds": 8.16,
      "text": "Both, really. The left a bit more. I've had the aids for about four years. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.58,
      "end_seconds": 47.88,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "When did you last have them checked? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.31,
      "end_seconds": 60.47,
      "duration_seconds": 10.16,
      "text": "Two years ago, at the hospital. They said the hearing was a bit worse, and adjusted the settings. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.42,
      "end_seconds": 69.82,
      "duration_seconds": 6.4,
      "text": "Are they working, do you think, or has something changed? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.27,
      "end_seconds": 80.72,
      "duration_seconds": 7.45,
      "text": "They whistle sometimes, and the batteries, I've been changing them every four days. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.7,
      "end_seconds": 88.1,
      "duration_seconds": 5.4,
      "text": "That's worth checking. Four days is short. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.43,
      "end_seconds": 94.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "That's what I thought. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.47,
      "end_seconds": 103.84,
      "duration_seconds": 5.37,
      "text": "Tell me about your general health. Anything long-term?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.14,
      "end_seconds": 110.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "Only the hearing loss. I'm seventy-three, you know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.09,
      "end_seconds": 130.82,
      "duration_seconds": 8.73,
      "text": "Let me check your pulse and blood pressure quickly. Pulse 72, blood pressure 130 over 80."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.81,
      "end_seconds": 136.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Normal for my age? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.07,
      "end_seconds": 155.34,
      "duration_seconds": 15.27,
      "text": "Very good. Now, I'd like to explain how I'd approach this. First, the hearing aids themselves. They can get clogged with wax, and the tubes can go stiff. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.92,
      "end_seconds": 160.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "Right. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.49,
      "end_seconds": 172.72,
      "duration_seconds": 9.23,
      "text": "Second, wax in the ear canal can block sound, and make the aids whistle. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.28,
      "end_seconds": 180.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.64,
      "text": "I haven't had my ears cleaned in years. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.62,
      "end_seconds": 194.25,
      "duration_seconds": 9.63,
      "text": "Third, the batteries. If they run out that quickly, there may be a problem with the aid itself. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.14,
      "end_seconds": 199.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Can you fix it? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.41,
      "end_seconds": 209.71,
      "duration_seconds": 8.3,
      "text": "Not here, but the audiology department can. I'll write to them with what you've told me. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 212.99,
      "end_seconds": 217.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "How long will that take? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.5,
      "end_seconds": 230.36,
      "duration_seconds": 10.86,
      "text": "A couple of weeks for the appointment. In the meantime, keep the aids dry, and wipe them each night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 232.42,
      "end_seconds": 235.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "I do that already. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.83,
      "end_seconds": 245.45,
      "duration_seconds": 7.62,
      "text": "Good. Don't use cotton buds in your ears, either, it pushes the wax deeper."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.78,
      "end_seconds": 251.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "I've never used them. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.06,
      "end_seconds": 261.67,
      "duration_seconds": 6.61,
      "text": "Good. Keep the television at a level your wife can tolerate. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.18,
      "end_seconds": 268.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Ha. That's a tall order. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.13,
      "end_seconds": 274.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Use subtitles, they help enormously. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 278.18,
      "end_seconds": 282.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "My daughter said the same. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.69,
      "end_seconds": 288.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "Sensible daughter. Anything else? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 292.02,
      "end_seconds": 295.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "No, I must dash. Thanks, doctor. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.19,
      "end_seconds": 301.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Bye. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 304.69,
      "end_seconds": 306.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "Bye. ~"
    }
  ]
}
